    "updated_at": "2015-08-31T10:38:45Z",
    "body": "> I guess there's no way to actually have pull requests be resolved automatically?\n\nPutting `Fixes #NN` into the (possibly amended) commit summary of the (final) commit (the one you actually push) would do that. I think that's the typical way to do it. But I think @domenic would like that it not be done that way. (And maybe there's something I'm not understanding that makes it bad for the case of this repo.)\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
