    "created_at": "2015-08-31T14:55:29Z",
    "updated_at": "2015-08-31T14:55:29Z",
    "body": "Pull requests get automatically marked as \"merged\" (purple) instead of \"closed\" (red) when they are based directly on top of the current master and get fast-forward merged. I force this to happen by ensuring my branches are always on top of current master before I merge them.\n\nYou can also do what @sideshowbarker suggests and edit the commit messages for PRs to say `Fixes #NN` or `Closes #NN` where `#NN` is the number of the pull request itself. But I find it weird to say \"here is pull request NN, it fixes itself.\" I don't feel too strongly though.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
